From bda16151b758fcc9a6027f07dd3a71dcf0a108db Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Theorem Labs
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 23:23:58 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [sanitizer_common] read gethostbyaddr's length as the
 socklen_t it is
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

🤖: The second argument of gethostbyaddr and gethostbyaddr_r is a socklen_t --
in musl, in glibc and in POSIX -- and the interceptors declare it int.  The
width is the same, so nothing truncates, but the value is not merely passed
through: it is the size of the range the interceptor marks as read.

  COMMON_INTERCEPTOR_READ_RANGE(ctx, addr, len);

READ_RANGE takes a uptr, so a length with the top bit set sign-extends to
something near 2^64 and the sanitizer reports on a program that read nothing
out of bounds:

  gethostbyaddr(malloc(4), 0x80000004u, AF_INET);
  ==742==ERROR: AddressSanitizer: negative-size-param: (size=-2147483644)

No real caller passes a length above 2GB -- it is 4 or 16 -- so this is a
report that cannot be provoked by accident, and it is not specific to musl.
It is still a wrong answer from an unmodified program, and the fix is the
declaration.
---
 .../lib/sanitizer_common/sanitizer_common_interceptors.inc  | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/compiler-rt/lib/sanitizer_common/sanitizer_common_interceptors.inc b/compiler-rt/lib/sanitizer_common/sanitizer_common_interceptors.inc
index a91bd64e8..bbd7a1c13 100644
--- a/compiler-rt/lib/sanitizer_common/sanitizer_common_interceptors.inc
+++ b/compiler-rt/lib/sanitizer_common/sanitizer_common_interceptors.inc
@@ -2959,8 +2959,8 @@ INTERCEPTOR(struct __sanitizer_hostent *, gethostbyname, char *name) {
   return res;
 }
 
-INTERCEPTOR(struct __sanitizer_hostent *, gethostbyaddr, void *addr, int len,
-            int type) {
+INTERCEPTOR(struct __sanitizer_hostent *, gethostbyaddr, void *addr,
+            unsigned len, int type) {
   void *ctx;
   COMMON_INTERCEPTOR_ENTER(ctx, gethostbyaddr, addr, len, type);
   COMMON_INTERCEPTOR_READ_RANGE(ctx, addr, len);
@@ -3046,7 +3046,7 @@ INTERCEPTOR(int, gethostent_r, struct __sanitizer_hostent *ret, char *buf,
 #endif
 
 #if SANITIZER_INTERCEPT_GETHOSTBYADDR_R
-INTERCEPTOR(int, gethostbyaddr_r, void *addr, int len, int type,
+INTERCEPTOR(int, gethostbyaddr_r, void *addr, unsigned len, int type,
             struct __sanitizer_hostent *ret, char *buf, SIZE_T buflen,
             __sanitizer_hostent **result, int *h_errnop) {
   void *ctx;
